---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { BUSINESS } from '../config';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Base
  title="What We Stand For | Stone's Throw Coffee in South Knoxville"
  description="Stone's Throw Coffee is a queer-centered, sober, accessible coffee shop and community space in South Knoxville. Here's what we stand for, and what we stand against."
>
  <section class="section section--pine">
    <div class="wrap" style="text-align: center;">
      <p class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--honey);">What We Stand For</p>
      <h1 style="color: var(--cream); max-width: 24ch; margin-inline: auto;">
        Community-centered coffee, just a Stone&rsquo;s Throw away.
      </h1>
      <p style="color: #e9e0cb; max-width: 50ch; margin-inline: auto; font-size: 1.1rem;">
        Change can start with conversations around a quality cup of coffee.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose values-prose">
      <p>
        {BUSINESS.name} is not politically neutral about human dignity.
      </p>
      <p>
        We are a queer-centered, sober, accessible coffee shop and community space in South
        Knoxville. Our values are not vague. They shape who we protect, what we platform, how we
        hire, how we partner, what books we carry, what events we host, and what behavior we
        refuse to normalize.
      </p>
      <p>
        We stand for LGBTQIA2S+ liberation, racial justice, reproductive freedom, bodily
        autonomy, disability justice, climate justice, immigrant dignity, labor rights, public
        education, banned books, religious freedom, mutual aid, harm reduction, sober community,
        and the right of every person to live safely and honestly.
      </p>
      <p>
        We stand against racism, fascism, white supremacy, Christian nationalism, antisemitism,
        Islamophobia, homophobia, transphobia, misogyny, ableism, xenophobia, forced-birth
        politics, book banning, anti-science extremism, conspiracy culture, and any movement that
        treats marginalized people as threats instead of neighbors.
      </p>

      <h2>We are anti-racist</h2>
      <p>
        Stone&rsquo;s Throw Coffee believes racism is not only individual prejudice. It is also
        systemic. It lives in housing, policing, schools, health care, wages, churches,
        workplaces, media, and public policy.
      </p>
      <p>
        We are committed to building a space where Black, Indigenous, Latino, Asian, immigrant,
        multiracial, and other people of color are safe, respected, represented, and heard.
      </p>
      <p>
        Anti-racism is not a slogan. It affects our shelves, our hiring, our vendor choices, our
        event calendar, our partnerships, and our willingness to listen when people tell us harm
        has happened.
      </p>

      <h2>We are anti-fascist</h2>
      <p>
        We oppose fascism, authoritarianism, political intimidation, forced conformity,
        censorship, scapegoating, and the worship of power over people.
      </p>
      <p>
        A queer-centered space cannot be neutral about fascism. Fascist movements have always
        targeted queer people, trans people, disabled people, immigrants, religious minorities,
        artists, educators, organizers, workers, and anyone who refuses to obey the approved
        script.
      </p>
      <p>Stone&rsquo;s Throw Coffee stands with communities targeted by authoritarian politics.</p>

      <h2>We are pro-choice and pro-reproductive freedom</h2>
      <p>We believe every person deserves bodily autonomy.</p>
      <p>
        Stone&rsquo;s Throw Coffee supports abortion access, contraception, miscarriage care,
        fertility care, gender-affirming care, accurate sex education, and honest medical
        information.
      </p>
      <p>
        Reproductive freedom is health care. It is economic justice. It is gender justice. It is
        queer justice. It is a basic part of human dignity.
      </p>
      <p>
        We reject shame-based politics that reduce people to their pregnancies, bodies, private
        medical choices, or ability to reproduce.
      </p>

      <h2>We are LGBTQIA2S+ centered</h2>
      <p>We are not simply &ldquo;friendly.&rdquo; We are queer-centered.</p>
      <p>
        Stone&rsquo;s Throw Coffee affirms queer love, trans lives, nonbinary identity, Two-Spirit
        people, asexual and aromantic people, intersex people, chosen family, drag, queer
        history, gender-expansive expression, and the right of every person to be named,
        addressed, and treated with dignity.
      </p>
      <p>
        Trans people are not a debate. We believe in respecting names, pronouns, privacy, medical
        autonomy, and public safety. We will not host or platform anti-trans rhetoric, and we
        will not treat bigotry as &ldquo;both sides.&rdquo;
      </p>
      <p>
        We reject the idea that queer people should be tolerated only when we are quiet,
        marketable, respectable, or easy to digest.
      </p>
      <p>Queer people belong here fully.</p>

      <h2>We are pro-worker</h2>
      <p>
        Stone&rsquo;s Throw Coffee believes workers deserve fair pay, safe conditions,
        predictable expectations, rest, respect, and freedom from harassment and exploitation.
      </p>
      <p>
        Coffee should not depend on burnout. Hospitality workers are not disposable. Baristas,
        cleaners, cooks, artists, musicians, makers, organizers, and vendors all deserve dignity.
      </p>
      <p>
        We support labor rights, unions, living wages, paid leave, and an economy built around
        people instead of corporate greed.
      </p>

      <h2>We believe housing is a human right</h2>
      <p>People cannot thrive without shelter.</p>
      <p>
        Stone&rsquo;s Throw Coffee believes housing is a human right, not a luxury product for
        landlords, developers, and corporations to exploit.
      </p>
      <p>
        We support affordable housing, tenant protections, unhoused community care, and public
        investment that keeps people alive and housed.
      </p>
      <p>
        A coffee shop cannot solve the housing crisis by itself. But we can refuse to treat
        poverty as a personal failure. We can support mutual aid. We can partner with people doing
        the work. We can make sure our language, policies, and community resources reflect the
        dignity of unhoused and housing-insecure neighbors.
      </p>

      <h2>We believe health care is a human right</h2>
      <p>
        Health care should not depend on wealth, employment, gender, zip code, or
        insurance-company permission.
      </p>
      <p>
        Stone&rsquo;s Throw Coffee supports universal health care, mental health care,
        reproductive health care, gender-affirming care, disability care, addiction recovery
        support, harm reduction, vaccines, and evidence-based medicine.
      </p>
      <p>
        We reject medical conspiracy theories, anti-vaccine fearmongering, wellness scams, and
        spiritual abuse that tells people to pray away conditions that deserve care.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our space may be planty, inclusive, herbal, and cozy. That does not mean anti-science.
        Comfort and ritual can coexist with medicine. Tea and herbs can sit beside vaccines and
        therapy. Magic does not require misinformation.
      </p>

      <h2>We are pro-immigrant</h2>
      <p>Immigrants are our neighbors.</p>
      <p>
        Stone&rsquo;s Throw Coffee supports immigrant dignity, refugee safety, asylum rights,
        family unity, language access, and a humane path to citizenship.
      </p>
      <p>
        We reject xenophobia, border cruelty, detention profiteering, and political narratives
        that blame immigrants for problems created by greed, racism, and bad policy.
      </p>

      <h2>We are climate-justice centered</h2>
      <p>
        We believe climate change is real, urgent, and inseparable from racial justice, economic
        justice, disability justice, food justice, and housing justice.
      </p>
      <p>
        Stone&rsquo;s Throw Coffee supports climate action, sustainable choices, local
        partnerships, waste reduction, public investment, and a livable future for ordinary
        people, not just the wealthy.
      </p>
      <p>We are not interested in greenwashing. We are interested in responsibility.</p>

      <h2>We are anti-censorship and pro-banned books</h2>
      <p>Stone&rsquo;s Throw Coffee believes people deserve access to books that tell the truth.</p>
      <p>
        We support banned books, queer books, Black history, feminist writing, labor history,
        disability writing, religious critique, survivor stories, Appalachian voices, and
        literature that helps people think freely.
      </p>
      <p>
        Book bans are rarely about protecting children. They are usually about controlling which
        people, histories, bodies, families, and ideas are allowed to exist in public.
      </p>
      <p>Our shelves will reflect curiosity, courage, and liberation.</p>

      <h2>We oppose Christian nationalism and religious extremism</h2>
      <p>Stone&rsquo;s Throw Coffee welcomes people of many faiths and people of no faith.</p>
      <p>
        We oppose Christian nationalism, religious extremism, spiritual abuse, forced belief,
        purity culture, anti-LGBTQIA2S+ theology, misogynistic theology, and the use of religion
        to control bodies, families, schools, libraries, workplaces, or public policy.
      </p>
      <p>
        Faith should never be used as a weapon against someone&rsquo;s safety, autonomy, or civil
        rights.
      </p>

      <h2>We believe public safety means care</h2>
      <p>
        Real public safety is not built by criminalizing poverty, queerness, disability,
        addiction, homelessness, or mental illness.
      </p>
      <p>
        Stone&rsquo;s Throw Coffee believes safer communities come from housing, health care,
        food access, living wages, education, mental health support, addiction recovery
        resources, harm reduction, and strong community relationships.
      </p>
      <p>We believe in accountability when harm happens. But we reject cruelty disguised as order.</p>

      <h2>We believe in mutual aid</h2>
      <p>Charity asks, &ldquo;What can I spare?&rdquo;</p>
      <p>Mutual aid asks, &ldquo;What do we owe each other?&rdquo;</p>
      <p>Stone&rsquo;s Throw Coffee believes in the second question.</p>
      <p>
        We will support practical community care whenever possible: resource shelves, hygiene
        items, food support partnerships, sober social events, local fundraisers, banned-book
        access, community education, and space for people doing the hard work of keeping each
        other alive.
      </p>

      <h2>We are a safe space with boundaries</h2>
      <p>Stone&rsquo;s Throw Coffee will be warm, but not passive.</p>
      <p>
        We will not allow harassment, threats, hate speech, stalking, intimidation, predatory
        behavior, racism, homophobia, transphobia, ableism, misogyny, fascist organizing, or
        religious harassment in our space.
      </p>
      <p>You do not have to agree with everyone in the room.</p>
      <p>You do have to respect their humanity.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--pine" aria-labelledby="values-cta-heading">
    <div class="wrap" style="text-align: center;">
      <h2 id="values-cta-heading" style="color: var(--cream);">Our bottom line</h2>
      <div class="prose" style="margin-inline: auto; text-align: left;">
        <p style="color: #e9e0cb;">
          Stone&rsquo;s Throw Coffee is for people who believe another kind of community is
          possible.
        </p>
        <p style="color: #e9e0cb;">
          Queerer. Kinder. Stranger. Braver. More accessible. More honest. More rooted in care
          than control.
        </p>
        <p style="color: #e9e0cb;">
          We are here for coffee. We are here for books. We are here for chosen family. We are
          here for workers. We are here for banned stories. We are here for reproductive freedom.
          We are here for sober joy. We are here for people who need a place to land.
        </p>
        <p style="color: var(--honey); font-family: var(--font-display); font-style: italic; font-size: 1.15rem;">
          Belonging should not be rare. It should be just a Stone&rsquo;s Throw away.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="btn-row" style="justify-content: center; margin-top: var(--space-3);">
        <a class="btn btn--solid" href={BUSINESS.gofundme} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Support the GoFundMe
        </a>
        <a class="btn btn--outline" href={`${base}/contact/`}>Get in touch</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
